## Context
Successor of ticket 1145 (closed as superseded, 2026-10-20). Author decision of 2026-10-20 (1146): transcript recovery stays out. PR #1528 merged with a capture failure: the /gaze verdict named "agents=6, same model family" and no seats, so no reviewer lines could be written. Advice (Fable, 2026-10-20): the forward path is the write-time ledger that PR #1521 (ticket 1142) already introduces, `scripts/review_evidence.py` records under `tickets/reviews/<base>..<head>/`. Verbatim model ids stay `model-state=runtime-masked` unless the runtime states them.

## Exit criteria
Rescoped by the author's decision on 2026-10-21 (trust the orchestrator; no per-seat record, floor or plan:
tickets 1176 and 1144). The point of the ticket stands: a review result must say which seats ran, so that
`/roar` can write the reviewer lines.
- [ ] The review result comment lists each seat that ran, with its role, its model family and the model id as
      observed from the launch (or `not observed`), and says which seats were skipped or failed.
- [ ] `/roar` appends the `reviewer:` attribution lines to the PR body from that list, without recovering
      anything from transcripts (decision 1146 of 2026-10-20 stands), and states a capture failure when the
      list is missing a seat.
- [ ] Positive control: a review whose seats are listed independently is reproduced exactly by the appended
      lines.
- [ ] Done after ticket 1144 (the fold of `review-pr` into `gaze`), since both define the result contract.
